# 136. Final Principle

The most important QA rule for AEGIS is:

> **Never test only whether the interface displays the correct thing. Test whether the entire system earned the right to display it.**

A number on a dashboard may have passed rendering tests while:

```text
the source was stale
the data was corrupted
the state was wrong
the model misunderstood it
the user lacked permission
the recommendation was unsupported
```

Therefore AEGIS quality must always be evaluated from:

```text
SOURCE
 ↓
DATA
 ↓
PROCESSING
 ↓
INTELLIGENCE
 ↓
STATE
 ↓
UI
 ↓
HUMAN DECISION
 ↓
OUTCOME
```

That is the complete chain that must be trustworthy.
